  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The first floor rear extension, by reason of its excessive bulking and massing, would not appear subservient to the main dwellinghouse but would appear an overly dominant addition in relation to the size of the modest semi-detached dwelling. Furthermore, its flat roof design would present a discordant feature that does not reflect the pitched roof design of the host dwelling and terrace row. &amp;nbsp;As such, the proposed development is contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (August 2026) - Policies D1, D4 and D6 of the London Plan (March 2021) - Policies DMD1, DMD5 and&amp;nbsp; SP2&amp;nbsp; of&amp;nbsp; The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024) - The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)&lt;/span&gt;",
    "&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(51, 51, 51);&quot;&gt;The scale, siting and design of the proposed development would result in an unacceptable loss of daylight, overshadowing and overbearing impacts to no.13 Charles Road. Therefore, the proposal would constitute unneighbourly development which is contrary to: - National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (August 2026); - Policy D6 of the London Plan (March 2021); - Policies DMD1, DMD5 and DMSI3 of&amp;nbsp; The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024); and - The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)&lt;/span&gt;"
  ]
}